; frost_cliffs.room - Penhascos: the bench in a cave under the west crag (cols 1-12, rows 41-44), then the climb to
; the cliff top (row 9) and the lighthouse (design 04 section 3.3). No gate: base kit, single jumps, no earth.
; WORLD-45 ("o level design da parte que sobe ao farol pode ser melhorado, não apenas várias plataformas flutuantes",
; user, 2026-11-16; reopened "Yes, after STORY-34", 2026-11-17): four parts, all ground that grows out of rock -
; a slope of uneven rock steps rising east from the cave (cols 15-36) to a landing (row 31); a chimney between the
; rock mass and the east wall: a rock step (cols 37-38, top 28), then a corbel on the mass (cols 34-35, row 25,
; one row so a jump from under it still reaches the step);
; a path under the top slab rising west on uneven treads (rows 21 to 16), under the slab's lip (cols 6-7) into a
; west chimney; a rock step at the west wall (cols 1-3, top 13) up onto the slab (from col 6), which runs east to
; the exit (row 8).
; A [secret] niche in the crag over the bench cave (cols 9-12, rows 38-39, cracked at col 12) holds a reward slot (`$`,
; WORLD-35); one jump from the slope's first step (row 41).
; Row 0 closed: a drawn rock ceiling over a room inside rock (WORLD-34, "Drawn rock ceiling, all five (Recommended)", user, 2026-10-14).

